Answer RSSI_BOUNDS (get 106): wifid's auto-join minimum RSSI comes from the driver and was 0.
With 1134 wifid kept the scan results but rejected every candidate: "Join candidate ... is not allowed
(error=(1 'Below minimum RSSI threshold'))" at rssi -61 and -77 (boot 1134). wifid reads ioctl 106 once at start
(Apple80211CopyValue 0x6a: RSSI_MIN, RSSI_MAX, RSSI_THRESHOLD; "Device RSSI bounds (%d, %d) with treshold (%d)",
wifid 0x10006186c) and copies RSSI_THRESHOLD into the device manager's auto-join threshold (wifid 0x1001872e0); the
stand-in answered EOPNOTSUPP, so the threshold was 0 and every real RSSI was below it. IO80211 reads
{u32 version; s32 min @4; s32 max @8; s32 threshold @12}. Values: -100 / 0 / -80 (wifid's own bad-RSSI threshold).

